source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-24
observed: A heading level is one digit, so `h10.` is text with or without a space after it; jiro keeps the line literal and warns rather than guessing a level.
-- input.jira --
h10.x
-- rendered.html --
<p>h10.x</p>
-- want.md --
h10.x
-- warnings.json --
[
  {"Line":1,"Column":1,"Construct":"heading","Reason":"malformed Jira heading remains literal"}
]
